Privacy Policy - MiniHabits

Last updated: October 30, 2026. Applies to MiniHabits 2.1.0 and later for Android. (Versión en español más abajo.)

Controller: TLL Studios (TLL Developers). Contact: tll.developers.apps@gmail.com

Summary
Your habits never leave your phone. MiniHabits has no account and no server of its own. The free plan shows ads (Google AdMob) and the app uses Google Analytics for Firebase and Firebase Crashlytics for aggregated usage statistics and crash reports.

What MiniHabits stores
Your habits, their history, your daily mood (if you log it) and your settings are stored only on this device. If Google backup is enabled on your Android phone, the system may include this data in your personal backup.

Backups
A daily automatic copy is saved on the device itself and the last 7 are kept. When you export a copy, a file is created that you choose where to save. MiniHabits does not send it anywhere.

Reminders and widgets
Reminders show the habit name; on the lock screen they appear according to your Android settings. If you add a widget (Premium), your habit names and progress appear on the home screen, also when fingerprint lock is on. This data is stored only on the device.

Ads (free plan)
The free plan shows a Google AdMob banner. In the European Union we ask for your consent before showing ads. Google may use the device advertising ID, approximate location derived from the IP address, device and app-set identifiers, ad interaction information and diagnostics, for advertising, analytics and fraud prevention. You can change your consent in Settings > Privacy. With Premium the ads SDK is not loaded. You can also reset or delete your advertising ID in Android Settings > Google > Ads.

Usage statistics and crash reports
We use Google Analytics for Firebase to know, in aggregate, which features are used (for example whether the tutorial is completed or a habit is created). We never send the names of your habits, their content or your mood. This includes app interactions, the Firebase installation ID and, for purchases, a purchase event.
We use Firebase Crashlytics to receive crash reports (technical stack trace, device model, Android and app version) so that we can fix them. They do not include your habits or their content.

Data processed by third-party SDKs (as declared in Google Play Data safety)
- Google AdMob: advertising ID / app set ID and device identifiers, approximate location (from the IP address), ad interactions and diagnostics; shared with Google for advertising, analytics and fraud prevention.
- Firebase Analytics: app interactions, Firebase installation ID / device identifiers, purchase events; for analytics.
- Firebase Crashlytics: crash logs and diagnostics; for analytics and app stability.
Data sent to these services is encrypted in transit (TLS).

Purchases
Purchases are processed by Google Play. MiniHabits does not receive your payment details.

Permissions
- Internet: only for ads, usage statistics, crash reports and purchases.
- Notifications and exact alarms: only for your reminders.
- Fingerprint or PIN (optional): handled by Android; MiniHabits never receives your fingerprint.

Children
MiniHabits is not directed to children under 13.

Your rights and data deletion
You can export your data whenever you want, delete each habit, or uninstall the app to delete everything, automatic copies included. The app has no accounts, so there is nothing on our servers to delete; for data processed by Google AdMob and Firebase see https://policies.google.com/privacy, reset your advertising ID as described above, or write to tll.developers.apps@gmail.com. If you think your rights are not respected, you can complain to the Spanish Data Protection Agency (www.aepd.es).

Changes
We may update this policy. The date at the top shows the latest version.

